    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d671">

                <pb facs="0222" n="1340" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v15p2/pg1340"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/6–2353: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in
                        Korea</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d671-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >secret<lb/>niact</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1953-07-06T19:37:00-04:00">July 6, 1953—7:37
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>20. For Robertson from Secretary. Have carefully considered your #19<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d671-f2"/> and 061600Z.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d671-f3"/> President’s
                    June 16 [<hi rendition="#italic">6</hi>] letter<anchor n="4" xml:id="d671-f4"/>
                    offering security pact was informally cleared with Senate leaders and received
                    general public approval. Any present uncertainty as to Senate action is slight
                    and results from feeling in some quarters that President Rhee desires to commit
                    US to a reckless suicide pact. We are trying to eliminate this fear and I shall
                    be meeting early Tuesday with bipartisan Senate leaders and will then cable
                    further. What is needed most of all is for Rhee to give assurance that ROK is
                    dependable partner not committed to rash adventures.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d671-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d671-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram, drafted by Dulles, was repeated to Tokyo for Murphy and Clark as
                    telegram 51 and to Pusan as telegram 17.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d671-f2" n="2" xml:id="d671-f2-content">
